IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc21-nouns`
IMPORT `ccc21-part-19-absolute`
IMPORT `ccc21-part-18`

-- ccc21-tests-part-18-election.l4 -- tests for ss 535 to 536.1(6) (the election and the preliminary inquiry request). Expected values written by hand from the text, beside each assertion.
-- Argument order is the GIVEN order of the function under test.

§ `Fixtures: charges (s 535 the charge) and the facts section 553 asks`

`s 535 test facts: an offence section 553 does not name` MEANS
    `s 553 the charge` WITH
        `s 553 the accused is charged in an information` IS TRUE
        `s 553 the offence charged` IS `Provision of the Code` WITH `section` IS 267, `subsection` IS ""
        `s 553 the offence charged, as paragraph (a) names it` IS `s 553(a) an offence that paragraph (a) does not name`
        `s 553 the theft is theft of cattle` IS FALSE
        `s 553 the subject-matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument` IS FALSE
        `s 553 the alleged value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars` IS 0
        `s 553 how the accused is charged` IS `s 553(b) with the offence itself`
        `s 553 the offence is under paragraph 4(4)(a) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act` IS FALSE

`s 535 test facts: theft of 100 dollars` MEANS
    `s 553 the charge` WITH
        `s 553 the accused is charged in an information` IS TRUE
        `s 553 the offence charged` IS `Provision of the Code` WITH `section` IS 334, `subsection` IS ""
        `s 553 the offence charged, as paragraph (a) names it` IS `s 553(a)(i) theft`
        `s 553 the theft is theft of cattle` IS FALSE
        `s 553 the subject-matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument` IS FALSE
        `s 553 the alleged value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars` IS 100
        `s 553 how the accused is charged` IS `s 553(b) with the offence itself`
        `s 553 the offence is under paragraph 4(4)(a) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act` IS FALSE

GIVEN class IS A `Class of offence`
      mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      imprisonment IS AN Imprisonment
      facts IS A `s 553 the charge`
GIVETH A `s 535 the charge`
`s 535 test charge` MEANS
    `s 535 the charge` WITH
        `s 535 the class of the offence charged` IS class
        `s 535 the mode in which the prosecutor proceeds` IS mode
        `s 535 the maximum imprisonment for the offence on indictment` IS imprisonment
        `s 535 the facts that bear on absolute jurisdiction` IS facts

-- A: indictable, 14 years, not absolute. B: indictable, ten years. C: indictable, life. D: indictable, ten years, absolute (theft of $100).
-- E: summary only. F: hybrid, prosecuted by indictment, ten years. G: hybrid, prosecuted summarily. H: indictable, no maximum stated. I: hybrid, by indictment, 14 years.
`s 535 test charge A` MEANS `s 535 test charge` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`) `s 535 test facts: an offence section 553 does not name`
`s 535 test charge B` MEANS `s 535 test charge` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`) `s 535 test facts: an offence section 553 does not name`
`s 535 test charge C` MEANS `s 535 test charge` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` `imprisonment for life` `s 535 test facts: an offence section 553 does not name`
`s 535 test charge D` MEANS `s 535 test charge` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`) `s 535 test facts: theft of 100 dollars`
`s 535 test charge E` MEANS `s 535 test charge` `an offence punishable on summary conviction` `on summary conviction` (`imprisonment for a term of` `six months`) `s 535 test facts: an offence section 553 does not name`
`s 535 test charge F` MEANS `s 535 test charge` `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction` `by indictment` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`) `s 535 test facts: an offence section 553 does not name`
`s 535 test charge G` MEANS `s 535 test charge` `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction` `on summary conviction` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`) `s 535 test facts: an offence section 553 does not name`
`s 535 test charge H` MEANS `s 535 test charge` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` `no imprisonment is stated` `s 535 test facts: an offence section 553 does not name`
`s 535 test charge I` MEANS `s 535 test charge` `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction` `by indictment` (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`) `s 535 test facts: an offence section 553 does not name`

§ `Tests -- section 535`

-- "punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment"
#ASSERT `s 535 an offence punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment` (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- exactly 14 years (boundary)
#ASSERT `s 535 an offence punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment` (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 14, 0, 0, TRUE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- 14 years less a day is below 14 years (boundary)
#ASSERT `s 535 an offence punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment` (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 15, 0, 0, TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- 15 years less a day is above 14 years
#ASSERT `s 535 an offence punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment` (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 13, 11, 30, FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- 13 years 11 months 30 days
#ASSERT `s 535 an offence punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment` (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 14, 0, 1, FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- 14 years and a day
#ASSERT `s 535 an offence punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment` (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 14, 1, 0, FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- 14 years and a month
#ASSERT `s 535 an offence punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 535 an offence punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment` `imprisonment for life` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 535 an offence punishable by 14 years or more of imprisonment` `no imprisonment is stated` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the maximum is not stated here
-- "an indictable offence"
#ASSERT `s 535 the offence charged is an indictable offence` `s 535 test charge A` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 535 the offence charged is an indictable offence` `s 535 test charge E` EQUALS FALSE   -- summary only
#ASSERT `s 535 the offence charged is an indictable offence` `s 535 test charge F` EQUALS TRUE   -- the core's third class, prosecuted by indictment (NOTES.md F4)
#ASSERT `s 535 the offence charged is an indictable offence` `s 535 test charge G` EQUALS FALSE   -- the same class, prosecuted summarily
-- the duty to inquire. Order: charge, before a justice, request made.
#ASSERT `s 535 the justice shall inquire into the charge` `s 535 test charge A` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 535 the justice shall inquire into the charge` `s 535 test charge C` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- life is 14 years or more
#ASSERT `s 535 the justice shall inquire into the charge` `s 535 test charge E` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not indictable
#ASSERT `s 535 the justice shall inquire into the charge` `s 535 test charge B` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- ten years: under 14
#ASSERT `s 535 the justice shall inquire into the charge` `s 535 test charge A` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not before a justice
#ASSERT `s 535 the justice shall inquire into the charge` `s 535 test charge A` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no request under 536(4) or 536.1(3)
#ASSERT `s 535 the justice shall inquire into the charge` `s 535 test charge H` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no maximum stated
#ASSERT `s 535 the justice shall inquire into the charge` `s 535 test charge H` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a definite no outranks a NOTHING
-- the extension to the other offence
#ASSERT `s 535 the inquiry extends to the other indictable offence` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 535 the inquiry extends to the other indictable offence` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an indictable offence
#ASSERT `s 535 the inquiry extends to the other indictable offence` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not the same transaction
#ASSERT `s 535 the inquiry extends to the other indictable offence` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not founded on the facts disclosed
#ASSERT `s 535 the inquiry extends to the other indictable offence` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 535 the inquiry extends to the other indictable offence` NOTHING TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 536(1), (2) and (2.1)`

-- 536(1): charge, who the accused is before.
#ASSERT `s 536(1) the justice shall remand the accused to appear before a provincial court judge` `s 535 test charge D` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 536(1) the justice shall remand the accused to appear before a provincial court judge` `s 535 test charge D` `s 536(1) a provincial court judge` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- before a provincial court judge already
#ASSERT `s 536(1) the justice shall remand the accused to appear before a provincial court judge` `s 535 test charge A` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not within section 553
#ASSERT `s 536(1) the justice shall remand the accused to appear before a provincial court judge` `s 535 test charge D` `s 536(1) someone who is not a justice` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 536(2): class. Order: charge, who, s 469 answer.
#ASSERT `s 536(2) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2)` `s 535 test charge A` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 536(2) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2)` `s 535 test charge A` `s 536(1) a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a provincial court judge is a justice
#ASSERT `s 536(2) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2)` `s 535 test charge I` `s 536(1) a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- hybrid prosecuted by indictment
#ASSERT `s 536(2) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2)` `s 535 test charge C` `s 536(1) a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- life
#ASSERT `s 536(2) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2)` `s 535 test charge A` `s 536(1) someone who is not a justice` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(2) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2)` `s 535 test charge E` `s 536(1) a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- summary
#ASSERT `s 536(2) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2)` `s 535 test charge G` `s 536(1) a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- hybrid prosecuted summarily
#ASSERT `s 536(2) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2)` `s 535 test charge B` `s 536(1) a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- ten years
#ASSERT `s 536(2) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2)` `s 535 test charge A` `s 536(1) a provincial court judge` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "other than an offence listed in section 469"
#ASSERT `s 536(2) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2)` `s 535 test charge B` `s 536(1) a provincial court judge` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- under 14 years outranks the section 469 answer
#ASSERT `s 536(2) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2)` `s 535 test charge H` `s 536(1) a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no maximum stated
#ASSERT `s 536(2) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2)` `s 535 test charge A` `s 536(1) a provincial court judge` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 469 not settled
-- 536(2) duty: the answer of the class function, information read.
#ASSERT `s 536(2) the justice shall put the accused to an election in the words of subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 536(2) the justice shall put the accused to an election in the words of subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "after the information has been read"
#ASSERT `s 536(2) the justice shall put the accused to an election in the words of subsection (2)` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(2) the justice shall put the accused to an election in the words of subsection (2)` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 536(2) the justice shall put the accused to an election in the words of subsection (2)` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 536(2.1): class. Order: charge, who, s 469 answer.
#ASSERT `s 536(2.1) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2.1)` `s 535 test charge B` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 536(2.1) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2.1)` `s 535 test charge A` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- 14 years or more is (2)'s
#ASSERT `s 536(2.1) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2.1)` `s 535 test charge B` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- listed in section 469 and under 14 years
#ASSERT `s 536(2.1) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2.1)` `s 535 test charge D` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- absolute jurisdiction under section 553
#ASSERT `s 536(2.1) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2.1)` `s 535 test charge E` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not indictable
#ASSERT `s 536(2.1) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2.1)` `s 535 test charge B` `s 536(1) someone who is not a justice` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(2.1) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2.1)` `s 535 test charge H` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 536(2.1) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2.1)` `s 535 test charge B` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 469 not settled
#ASSERT `s 536(2.1) the accused is one referred to in subsection (2.1)` `s 535 test charge A` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- 14 years or more settles it
-- 536(2.1) duty
#ASSERT `s 536(2.1) the justice shall put the accused to an election in the words of subsection (2.1)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 536(2.1) the justice shall put the accused to an election in the words of subsection (2.1)` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(2.1) the justice shall put the accused to an election in the words of subsection (2.1)` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(2.1) the justice shall put the accused to an election in the words of subsection (2.1)` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the words: copied from the text
#ASSERT `s 536(2) the words in which the justice puts the accused to an election` EQUALS "You have the option to elect to be tried by a provincial court judge without a jury and without having had a preliminary inquiry; or you may elect to be tried by a judge without a jury; or you may elect to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you do not elect now, you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you elect to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury or if you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury, you will have a preliminary inquiry only if you or the prosecutor requests one. How do you elect to be tried?"
#ASSERT `s 536(2.1) the words in which the justice puts the accused to an election` EQUALS "You have the option to elect to be tried by a provincial court judge without a jury; or you may elect to be tried by a judge without a jury; or you may elect to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you do not elect now, you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. How do you elect to be tried?"
#ASSERT `s 536.1(2) the words in which the judge or justice of the peace puts the accused to an election` EQUALS "You have the option to elect to be tried by a judge without a jury or to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you do not elect now, you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you elect to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury or if you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury, you will have a preliminary inquiry only if you or the prosecutor requests one. How do you elect to be tried?"
#ASSERT `s 536.1(2.1) the words in which the judge or justice of the peace puts the accused to an election` EQUALS "You have the option to elect to be tried by a judge without a jury or to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you do not elect now, you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. How do you elect to be tried?"

§ `Tests -- section 536(3), (4) and following`

#ASSERT `s 536(3) the accused elects to be tried by a provincial court judge` (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 536(3) the accused elects to be tried by a provincial court judge` (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a judge without a jury`) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(3) the accused elects to be tried by a provincial court judge` `s 536(2) does not elect` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(3) the justice shall endorse on the information a record of the election` (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 536(3) the justice shall endorse on the information a record of the election` (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a court composed of a judge and jury`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(3) the justice shall endorse on the information a record of the election` `s 536(2) does not elect` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3)(a): answer, who
#ASSERT `s 536(3)(a) the justice shall remand the accused to appear and plead before a provincial court judge` (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge`) `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 536(3)(a) the justice shall remand the accused to appear and plead before a provincial court judge` (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge`) `s 536(1) a provincial court judge` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(3)(a) the justice shall remand the accused to appear and plead before a provincial court judge` (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge`) `s 536(1) someone who is not a justice` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 536(3)(a) the justice shall remand the accused to appear and plead before a provincial court judge` (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a judge without a jury`) `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3)(b): answer, who
#ASSERT `s 536(3)(b) the provincial court judge shall call on the accused to plead to the charge` (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge`) `s 536(1) a provincial court judge` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 536(3)(b) the provincial court judge shall call on the accused to plead to the charge` (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge`) `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(3)(b) the provincial court judge shall call on the accused to plead to the charge` (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge`) `s 536(1) someone who is not a justice` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 536(3)(b) the provincial court judge shall call on the accused to plead to the charge` `s 536(2) does not elect` `s 536(1) a provincial court judge` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(3)(b) the provincial court judge shall proceed with the trial or fix a time for the trial` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 536(3)(b) the provincial court judge shall proceed with the trial or fix a time for the trial` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the accused pleads guilty
#ASSERT `s 536(3)(b) the provincial court judge shall proceed with the trial or fix a time for the trial` (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(3)(b) the provincial court judge shall proceed with the trial or fix a time for the trial` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4): the recognizer. answer, deemed under 565(1)(a)
#ASSERT `s 536(4) the accused elects a judge without a jury or a judge and jury, or does not elect, or is deemed under paragraph 565(1)(a) to have elected a judge and jury` (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a judge without a jury`) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 536(4) the accused elects a judge without a jury or a judge and jury, or does not elect, or is deemed under paragraph 565(1)(a) to have elected a judge and jury` (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a court composed of a judge and jury`) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 536(4) the accused elects a judge without a jury or a judge and jury, or does not elect, or is deemed under paragraph 565(1)(a) to have elected a judge and jury` `s 536(2) does not elect` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 536(4) the accused elects a judge without a jury or a judge and jury, or does not elect, or is deemed under paragraph 565(1)(a) to have elected a judge and jury` (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge`) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(4) the accused elects a judge without a jury or a judge and jury, or does not elect, or is deemed under paragraph 565(1)(a) to have elected a judge and jury` (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge`) TRUE EQUALS TRUE   -- deemed under 565(1)(a)
-- (4): charge, who, s 469, answer, deemed, request, s 577
#ASSERT `s 536(4) the justice shall hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge` `s 535 test charge A` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a court composed of a judge and jury`) FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the accused elects a jury
#ASSERT `s 536(4) the justice shall hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge` `s 535 test charge A` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a judge without a jury`) FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the accused elects a judge alone
#ASSERT `s 536(4) the justice shall hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge` `s 535 test charge A` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) `s 536(2) does not elect` FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- does not elect
#ASSERT `s 536(4) the justice shall hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge` `s 535 test charge A` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge`) TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- deemed under paragraph 565(1)(a)
#ASSERT `s 536(4) the justice shall hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge` `s 535 test charge A` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge`) FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- elects a provincial court judge: no limb
#ASSERT `s 536(4) the justice shall hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge` `s 535 test charge A` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a court composed of a judge and jury`) FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no request
#ASSERT `s 536(4) the justice shall hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge` `s 535 test charge A` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` (JUST TRUE) (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge`) FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- second limb: an offence listed in section 469 punishable by 14 years or more
#ASSERT `s 536(4) the justice shall hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge` `s 535 test charge B` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` (JUST TRUE) (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge`) FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- listed in section 469 but under 14 years
#ASSERT `s 536(4) the justice shall hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge` `s 535 test charge A` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a court composed of a judge and jury`) FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- subject to section 577: a direct indictment has been preferred
#ASSERT `s 536(4) the justice shall hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge` `s 535 test charge A` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a court composed of a judge and jury`) FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 577 not settled
#ASSERT `s 536(4) the justice shall hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge` `s 535 test charge A` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` NOTHING (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a court composed of a judge and jury`) FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 469 not settled
#ASSERT `s 536(4) the justice shall hold a preliminary inquiry into the charge` `s 535 test charge H` `s 536(1) a justice other than a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a court composed of a judge and jury`) FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no maximum stated
-- (4.1): answer of the class function, answer, deemed
#ASSERT `s 536(4.1) the justice shall endorse on the information a statement of the election and of any request for a preliminary inquiry` (JUST TRUE) (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a judge without a jury`) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 536(4.1) the justice shall endorse on the information a statement of the election and of any request for a preliminary inquiry` (JUST TRUE) `s 536(2) does not elect` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 536(4.1) the justice shall endorse on the information a statement of the election and of any request for a preliminary inquiry` (JUST TRUE) (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge`) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(4.1) the justice shall endorse on the information a statement of the election and of any request for a preliminary inquiry` (JUST FALSE) `s 536(2) does not elect` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(4.1) the justice shall endorse on the information a statement of the election and of any request for a preliminary inquiry` NOTHING `s 536(2) does not elect` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 536(4.1) the justice shall also endorse the warrant of remand` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 536(4.1) the justice shall also endorse the warrant of remand` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not in custody
#ASSERT `s 536(4.1) the justice shall also endorse the warrant of remand` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(4.1) the justice shall also endorse the warrant of remand` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4.11): charge, who, s 469
#ASSERT `s 536(4.11) the justice shall endorse on the information a statement showing whether a preliminary inquiry has been requested` `s 535 test charge A` `s 536(1) a provincial court judge` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 536(4.11) the justice shall endorse on the information a statement showing whether a preliminary inquiry has been requested` `s 535 test charge A` `s 536(1) a provincial court judge` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not listed in section 469
#ASSERT `s 536(4.11) the justice shall endorse on the information a statement showing whether a preliminary inquiry has been requested` `s 535 test charge B` `s 536(1) a provincial court judge` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- under 14 years
#ASSERT `s 536(4.11) the justice shall endorse on the information a statement showing whether a preliminary inquiry has been requested` `s 535 test charge A` `s 536(1) someone who is not a justice` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(4.11) the justice shall endorse on the information a statement showing whether a preliminary inquiry has been requested` `s 535 test charge A` `s 536(1) a provincial court judge` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 536(4.11) the justice shall endorse on the information a statement showing whether a preliminary inquiry has been requested` `s 535 test charge H` `s 536(1) a provincial court judge` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 536(4.11) the justice shall also endorse the warrant of remand` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 536(4.11) the justice shall also endorse the warrant of remand` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(4.11) the justice shall also endorse the warrant of remand` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(4.11) the justice shall also endorse the warrant of remand` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4.12)
#ASSERT `s 536(4.12) the justice shall endorse on the information a statement showing the nature of the election` (JUST TRUE) (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a judge without a jury`) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 536(4.12) the justice shall endorse on the information a statement showing the nature of the election` (JUST TRUE) (`s 536(2) elects` `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge`) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(4.12) the justice shall endorse on the information a statement showing the nature of the election` (JUST FALSE) `s 536(2) does not elect` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(4.12) the justice shall endorse on the information a statement showing the nature of the election` NOTHING `s 536(2) does not elect` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 536(4.12) the justice shall also endorse the warrant of remand` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 536(4.12) the justice shall also endorse the warrant of remand` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(4.12) the justice shall also endorse the warrant of remand` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 536(4.12) the justice shall also endorse the warrant of remand` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4.2), (4.3), (5)
#ASSERT `s 536(4.2) a preliminary inquiry must be held with respect to all of them` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 536(4.2) a preliminary inquiry must be held with respect to all of them` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- one accused
#ASSERT `s 536(4.2) a preliminary inquiry must be held with respect to all of them` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- none requests
#ASSERT `s 536(4.3) the justice shall fix the date for the trial or the date on which the accused must appear in the trial court to have the date fixed` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- no request made
#ASSERT `s 536(4.3) the justice shall fix the date for the trial or the date on which the accused must appear in the trial court to have the date fixed` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a request is made
#ASSERT `s 536(5) the justice has jurisdiction for the purposes of subsection (4)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the first justice has not commenced to take evidence
#ASSERT `s 536(5) the justice has jurisdiction for the purposes of subsection (4)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- has commenced
#ASSERT `s 536(5) the justice has jurisdiction for the purposes of subsection (4)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a justice with no jurisdiction in the province

